I will not melee attack floating eyes, even though sure, 8 out of 10
times they die with one hit and I can eat the corpse to gain a certain
mental acuity.  I will remember that the other 2 out of 10 times my
10th level Valkryie is killed by a newt.

I will not wait until I have 10 hit points left before I engrave
Elbereth because then I often die with Elberath or Elberzth written in
dust under my feet.

I will not engrave Elbereth and then use my expensive camera so the
monsters can kill me when they're blind.

I will stop and wait when I am confused.  I will not slay my pet, bump
into the Oracle, or attack a shopkeeper.

I will not melee attack leprechauns because sure, 8 out of 10 times
they die with one hit.  I will remember that 2 out of 10 times they
lighten my purse and I spend a thousand turns chasing them all over
the level to get my money back.

I will remember that it's not worth nearly dying of hunger chasing a
leprechaun all over the level just to get 75 gold back.

I will remember to switch weapons before I #force a chest with
Mjollnir.

I will remember that dipping my longsword into a fountain is a great
way to get Excalibur at 5th level, but is also a great way to be
surrounded by poisonous snakes at 5th level.  I will remember not to
whine about this.






